From 453e0e0717f1092b205b6560041745a670b0a95b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Macktherealonereally <macdev@mackthessd.org>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:03:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] exynos2100: Stop the Codec2 decoders from outputting SBWC
 buffers

With vendor.debug.c2.sbwc.enable=true, the Exynos Codec2 decoders
(hardware/samsung_slsi-linaro/codec2, ExynosUtils::GetCompressedColorType
-> DecCommonCnv::cnvCompressedColor) use Samsung bandwidth-compressed
YUV for every IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED output surface. On exynos2100
USE_FLEXIBLE_P010 is unset, so that format is
HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_EXYNOS_YCbCr_420_SP_M_SBWC. The decoders do not check
whether the consumer can read that format.

Only the DPU can read SBWC. The Mali GPU cannot. One UI's SurfaceFlinger
calls the SBWC decompressor HAL before GPU composition, but AOSP
SurfaceFlinger has no such path. As soon as a video layer falls back to
client (GPU) composition, RenderEngine samples compressed data as if it
were plain YUV. Rounded corners always force client composition
(OutputLayer::isClientCompositionForced), and so can shadows and the
scaling during PiP enter/exit animations. This is the likely cause of
the flickering and blocky/pixelated frames in YouTube when the player
shrinks into PiP (XDA 4790286 #137).

Decode to uncompressed YUV instead. The same change was made in
exynos1480/android_device_samsung_a55x commit 238b6d680364 ("a55x:
Disable vendor.debug.c2.sbwc.enable"). The cost is some extra memory
bandwidth during video playback.

This only affects decoder output. The HWC's own M2M scaler output stays
SBWC (DEFAULT_MPP_DST_YUV_FORMAT in
libhwc2.1/platform/exynos2100/ExynosHWCModule.h:48), so this does not
touch the scaler/FBC error path that Floppy2100 works around in the
kernel. Encoders and the SBWC decompressor service are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vendor.prop | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vendor.prop b/vendor.prop
index 5684f38..e16837f 100644
--- a/vendor.prop
+++ b/vendor.prop
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ ro.vendor.hw.use_secure_encoder_only=1
 
 ## Codec2
 ro.vendor.gpu.dataspace=1
-vendor.debug.c2.sbwc.enable=true
+vendor.debug.c2.sbwc.enable=false
 debug.c2.use_dmabufheaps=1
 media.c2.dmabuf.padding=512
 debug.stagefright.c2inputsurface=-1
-- 
2.55.0

